# 100x100 App Guide

## Architecture
- Keep the app lightweight and mobile-first.
- Frontend is a single page in `index.html` (HTML, CSS, vanilla JS).
- Serverless endpoints live in `api/` (`/api/tts`, `/api/shout`).

## Frontend Conventions
- Preserve fast tap UX on `+/-` and avoid blocking the UI.
- Keep swimmer names fixed: `Carlijn`, `Guido`, `Rik`, `Saskia`, `Wouter`.
- Persist user state in `localStorage` (laps, voice toggle, selected voice).
- Maintain fallback behavior: if AI/voice APIs fail, app must still function.

## Voice and Shouts
- ElevenLabs voice selection comes from env-backed keys (`ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID*`).
- AI shout text should be short, fluent, family-friendly, and avoid swimmer names.
- UI already prefixes swimmer name; generated shout text should not repeat names.
- Keep cancellation logic for overlapping audio/speech to avoid noisy stacking.

## API and Security
- Never expose API keys in frontend code.
- Keep all provider calls in serverless routes (`api/*.js`).
- Validate and sanitize incoming text/body fields.
- Trim env vars before use to avoid newline/format issues.

## Deployment and Reliability
- Prefer deterministic defaults with graceful fallbacks.
- After behavior changes to voice/AI routes, verify via production endpoint tests.
- Keep docs in `README.md` aligned with required env vars.
- If tests pass; commit, push, deploy
